terminal-eaglercraft is three things. Only the first of them is in this
repository. Read this before copying any of it.

1. The wrapper, MIT (see LICENSE)
   bin/terminal-eaglercraft, install.sh, web/serve.mjs, web/look.js, scripts/*
   Written for this project. This is everything in this repository.

2. EaglercraftX 1.8, downloaded when you install, under its own terms
   web/client.html
   Eaglercraft is a browser port of Minecraft. It is not in this repository, it
   is not distributed by this project, and no part of it is redistributed here.
   scripts/fetch-client.sh downloads one file, from a URL pinned to an exact
   commit, and checks it against a pinned sha256 before using it. That file is
   an EaglercraftX 1.8 offline client from the Eaglercraft-Archive on GitHub,
   with EaglerForge's mod loader in it.

   That client contains decompiled Minecraft code. It is not ours, it is not
   MIT, and it is not ours to relicense or to redistribute. Whether you may
   have a copy of it is between you, its authors, and Mojang. Repositories
   hosting Eaglercraft have been taken down under the DMCA before, which is why
   this project downloads rather than ships, and why --client lets you point it
   at a copy you already have.

   The archive: https://github.com/Eaglercraft-Archive
   EaglerForge:  https://github.com/EaglerForge

